# Phase 4 Walkthrough: Financial Learning & Gamification

I have successfully executed the first phase of our massive Financial Learning & Rewards expansion!

## 🏗️ 1. Architecture Implementation
All 4 new backend microservices have been scaffolded and are ready for deep logic implementation:
- **`education-service`**: Scaffolded with Java/Spring Boot.
- **`event-service`**: Scaffolded with Java/Spring Boot.
- **`rewards-service`**: Scaffolded with Java/Spring Boot.
- **`notification-engine`**: Scaffolded with Spring Boot Mail integration for sending emails.

## ⚙️ 2. Gamification Logic (Education Service)
I have implemented the core Gamification logic in the backend:
- Created the `Course` and `Video` JPA Entities.
- Created the `LearningGamificationController` REST endpoint.
- **Business Rule Enforced**: Users must score >= 70% on interactive video quizzes to earn points.
- **Event-Driven**: Once a quiz is passed, the service calculates the earned points (Base + Bonus) and automatically publishes a `COURSE_COMPLETED` event payload directly into our Kafka message broker, which the Rewards Service will eventually listen to!

## 🎓 3. Frontend Web: The Learning Center
To bring this to life, I updated the React Web Dashboard to include the interactive **Learning Center**. 

It now features embedded video courses (e.g., YouTube) and an interactive gamification quiz prompt seamlessly integrated into the UI.

